WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.931
Your watch measures. Nura shows the working.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.666
Recovery compares last night with your own
previous twenty-eight nights. Open it

00:00:09.666 --> 00:00:14.182
to see heart-rate variability, sleeping
heart rate, and sleep, with the weights

00:00:14.182 --> 00:00:14.558
shown.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:20.736
Sleep looks beyond the hours. Duration,
regularity, and interruptions make up most

00:00:20.736 --> 00:00:25.307
of the score. Sleep need includes strain,
sleep debt, and naps.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:31.275
Strain tracks how much work your heart did,
on a zero-to-twenty-one scale. Harder

00:00:31.275 --> 00:00:36.001
minutes count more. Open a workout to
inspect heart-rate zones and training load.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:41.902
Health score combines fitness, activity,
sleep, and resting heart rate. See how

00:00:41.902 --> 00:00:43.165
each part contributes.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:50.841
Cardio compares your estimated fitness with
your age group, alongside heart-rate

00:00:50.841 --> 00:00:51.277
trends.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:57.508
The target planner shows how changes could
move your score, with the assumptions

00:00:57.508 --> 00:00:57.843
visible.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:06.640
Body Age estimates your habits in years
above or below your calendar age. It uses

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.957
six-month averages, with each factor shown.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:15.129
Inspect the formulas, weights, research, and
limitations behind each estimate.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.641
Your data, explained. Try Nura.
